            "description": "Master Thesis: To accelerate the battery simulation process for crash and impact test using ML.\n\n- The objective of this thesis was to predict internal short circuits in batteries under crash conditions. \n- A thermo-mechanical single-cell model was developed in Radioss for a single-point indentation test. This model was then utilized to generate datasets based on various design variables, with the entire process being fully automated using HyperStudy. \n- PhysicsAI, an Altair tool leveraging Graph Neural Networks (GNN) for predictive modeling, was employed to train a machine learning model to predict strain distributions within the battery model. The predicted strain values were subsequently validated against real-time experimental test results. \n- By using the thermo-mechanical framework, strain and temperature profiles were mapped, effectively illustrating the occurrence of internal short circuits within the battery system.",
